    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite consists of the single black-box `AcceptanceTest`, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year, following the existing patterns for the other derived owner fields (`customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are populated, set the membership number via a new `membershipNumber(...)` helper:\n   ```java\n   String yy = String.format(\"%02d\", registrationDate.getYear() % 100);\n   return customerCode + \"-M\" + yy;\n   ```\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it (and MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`) \u2014 Added the `membership_number` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column is required there.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` confirms the response's `membershipNumber` equals `customerCode + \"-M\" + yy` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).",
